1
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,159
I won't take it to heart.

2
00:00:38,679 --> 00:00:39,600
When it comes to my own life,

3
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:40,479
I know what I'm doing.

4
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:41,880
Don't take it to heart either.

5
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:18,879
What kind of caps are these? They're all ruined.

6
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:24,480
Director Cheng.

7
00:01:25,159 --> 00:01:26,159
What's up with you?

8
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:27,840
Plant's been shut down for two days,

9
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:29,040
and you've gotten rusty too?

10
00:01:36,799 --> 00:01:37,359
Shunzi.

11
00:01:38,319 --> 00:01:39,640
Two days without work,

12
00:01:40,239 --> 00:01:42,040
and Workshop Two hasn't raised hell?

13
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,120
Of course we have.

14
00:01:44,359 --> 00:01:45,400
Everyone's downed tools.

15
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:49,840
Director Cheng,

16
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:52,319
I heard Ma Guowen's out to settle scores,

17
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:54,280
especially with your bottling workshop.

18
00:01:54,719 --> 00:01:55,560
You'd better watch your back.

19
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,200
Someone definitely snitched.

20
00:01:58,879 --> 00:02:00,799
We've got a traitor among us.

21
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:03,480
I'm off.

22
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,039
This scarf is pretty nice.

23
00:03:59,039 --> 00:04:00,280
It's thick and warm.

24
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,400
It'll last you eight to ten years.

25
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,280
How much do you even make, anyway?

26
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,759
Why spend so much money on this?

27
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:08,039
Just tell me if I've got good taste.

28
00:04:08,319 --> 00:04:09,560
You're just buttering me up.

29
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,759
Just tell me, do you like it or not?

30
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:11,639
All right, I like it.

31
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:13,840
Who is it?

32
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,839
How come you still have my mom's key?

33
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:17,920
Haipeng?

34
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:20,240
Why'd you buy so much stuff again?

35
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:21,279
I'm telling you,

36
00:04:21,279 --> 00:04:23,040
the fridge is already packed full.

37
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,319
There's no room left.

38
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:25,319
I was just thinking...

39
00:04:25,319 --> 00:04:26,920
It got freezing cold outside,

40
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,160
so try not to go out unless you have to.

41
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:28,480
Okay.

42
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:30,319
If you really must go out,

43
00:04:30,519 --> 00:04:31,600
remember to bundle up in your thick coat.

44
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:33,680
What's this?

45
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:34,800
The fridge is full,

46
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:36,720
so I'll put it out on the balcony.

47
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:37,199
All right.

48
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,120
Haipeng.

49
00:04:40,319 --> 00:04:42,040
I want some apples and red dates.

50
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:42,519
Sure.

51
00:04:44,759 --> 00:04:45,680
What are you just standing there for?

52
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,319
Put that stuff out on the balcony for me.

53
00:04:47,959 --> 00:04:48,920
Let me do it. Let me do it.

54
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:49,879
You really are something.

55
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,120
Give it to me. Give it to me.

56
00:04:52,079 --> 00:04:53,000
I'll buy some for you later.

57
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:53,480
Okay.

58
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:54,639
Give it to me.

59
00:04:54,639 --> 00:04:55,160
I've got it.

60
00:04:57,319 --> 00:04:59,240
Liu Xuemei used to travel to Qingzhou often back then.

61
00:05:00,639 --> 00:05:02,319
Do you recall if she ever

62
00:05:02,319 --> 00:05:05,000
mentioned a Qingzhou cab driver?

63
00:05:07,639 --> 00:05:08,639
I don't think so.

64
00:05:10,279 --> 00:05:10,680
Besides,

65
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:12,720
that was a decade ago. How would I remember?

66
00:05:15,839 --> 00:05:16,800
What are you up to now?

67
00:05:17,639 --> 00:05:18,560
Nothing.

68
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,600
Let me tell you,

69
00:05:23,279 --> 00:05:24,120
a few days ago,

70
00:05:24,759 --> 00:05:26,079
Old Qian almost died.

71
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:27,800
Can't you just leave things alone?

72
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:31,759
Just get out of here.

73
00:05:33,319 --> 00:05:33,720
I'm leaving.

74
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:34,360
I've got things to do.

75
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,160
I'm heading out now.

76
00:05:36,399 --> 00:05:37,000
Haipeng,

77
00:05:37,319 --> 00:05:39,959
I was thinking we still need a freezer. What should we do?

78
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,079
Once the weather warms up,

79
00:05:42,079 --> 00:05:42,800
I'll get one for you.

80
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:43,560
Good, good, good.

81
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:45,160
Bundle up warm when you go outside!

82
00:05:45,519 --> 00:05:45,839
I'm off.

83
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:46,639
Take care!

84
00:05:47,319 --> 00:05:48,040
Xiaoqin.

85
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,199
Is your dad free today?

86
00:05:50,399 --> 00:05:51,399
I'd like to take him out for a meal.

87
00:05:52,439 --> 00:05:53,639
It's nothing.

88
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:56,319
Wasn't he director of the Commerce Bureau back then,

89
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:58,680
overseeing the brewery auction and all?

90
00:05:59,639 --> 00:06:00,519
I wanted to ask him a few questions.

91
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,720
All right, I'll wait to hear from you.

92
00:06:23,079 --> 00:06:23,480
Chuang.

93
00:06:24,439 --> 00:06:25,639
This is Chen Qingchun's car.

94
00:06:36,079 --> 00:06:36,360
Let's go.

95
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:41,800
Old Chen,

96
00:06:42,399 --> 00:06:43,720
what's wrong with you these days?

97
00:06:44,199 --> 00:06:45,120
You look completely out of it.

98
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,319
I crashed into that sculpture outside the brewery.

99
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:50,040
Now they want me to pay for it.

100
00:06:50,519 --> 00:06:52,120
It already cost me a fortune to fix my car!

101
00:06:52,839 --> 00:06:53,560
Later on,

102
00:06:53,639 --> 00:06:54,680
let's go grab a drink.

103
00:06:55,319 --> 00:06:56,240
Shake off this bad luck.

104
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,480
Not today.

105
00:06:58,480 --> 00:06:59,120
I'm not in the mood.

106
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:00,600
Liquor's the essence of grain!

107
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:02,000
The more you drink, the younger you stay!

108
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:03,279
Come on, let's go.

109
00:07:03,279 --> 00:07:03,879
Come with us.

110
00:07:05,279 --> 00:07:06,920
My in-laws are coming over today.

111
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,040
I've gotta get home early.

112
00:07:09,319 --> 00:07:11,079
Then invite the former director along too!

113
00:07:11,319 --> 00:07:12,240
He's already retired.

114
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,240
What's the point?

115
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:13,759
Some other day.

116
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:14,800
Come on.

117
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:15,639
Let's go, come on.

118
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:16,560
Who's Chen Qingchun?

119
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:25,959
Three plates of mutton,

120
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:28,040
frozen tofu, glass noodles,

121
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,120
and black fungus.

122
00:07:31,959 --> 00:07:32,680
Xiaoqin,

123
00:07:32,879 --> 00:07:34,360
between pickled cabbage and spinach,

124
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,399
which one do you prefer?

125
00:07:36,279 --> 00:07:37,480
Let's see what Leshui likes.

126
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,480
I'm good with anything, Uncle.

127
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,319
Then pickled cabbage and spinach,

128
00:07:40,319 --> 00:07:41,000
one order of each.

129
00:07:42,199 --> 00:07:43,639
Two plates of dumplings, too:

130
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,600
one pickled cabbage,

131
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,360
and one three-delicacy.

132
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:46,199
What about you two?

133
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:48,000
Want some sesame flatbread as well?

134
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:49,600
That's enough, Dad.

135
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:50,439
All right.

136
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,519
That should be plenty.

137
00:07:52,319 --> 00:07:53,079
All right, just a moment.

138
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:53,639
Uncle...

139
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,439
Wait.

140
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:55,240
Say...

141
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:57,000
you prepare dumpling dipping sauce, right?

142
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:57,920
Yes, we do.

143
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:58,959
Three dashes of vinegar,

144
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,079
two dashes of soy sauce,

145
00:08:00,439 --> 00:08:01,439
a spoonful of chili oil,

146
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:02,560
and a spoonful of minced garlic.

147
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:03,480
Sure thing, just a moment.

148
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:04,000
Make it quick!

149
00:08:06,759 --> 00:08:07,759
Shen Leshui.

150
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:09,480
Hello, Director Zheng.

151
00:08:10,399 --> 00:08:11,639
Drop the "Director."

152
00:08:11,959 --> 00:08:12,759
I'm retired.

153
00:08:14,879 --> 00:08:15,319
As for me,

154
00:08:15,319 --> 00:08:17,600
I really don't like people calling me "Director."

155
00:08:18,439 --> 00:08:20,279
Makes me feel out of touch with the people.

156
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:23,240
You can just call me Old Zheng.

157
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,680
Or Uncle, either is fine.

158
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:26,360
Xiaoqin knows that about me.

159
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:27,160
A guy like me,

160
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,079
I don't care for formalities.

161
00:08:28,839 --> 00:08:30,040
I like joking around.

162
00:08:31,519 --> 00:08:32,519
I'm easygoing.

163
00:08:34,159 --> 00:08:35,159
Dad, let's eat first.

164
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:36,919
Let me propose a toast.

165
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:38,600
Leshui.

166
00:08:38,879 --> 00:08:40,480
"The wise find joy in water."

167
00:08:40,799 --> 00:08:41,960
What a great name.

168
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:43,240
Thank you, Uncle.

169
00:08:43,679 --> 00:08:46,080
I've always respected cultured,

170
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:46,960
educated folks.

171
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:49,639
Comrade Shen Leshui is someone special now.

172
00:08:49,879 --> 00:08:52,840
A renowned journalist!

173
00:08:53,639 --> 00:08:54,279
And today,

174
00:08:54,279 --> 00:08:56,759
to have lunch with Comrade Shen Leshui,

175
00:08:56,879 --> 00:08:58,759
is truly a great joy of mine.

176
00:08:59,519 --> 00:09:00,000
Come on, Dad.

177
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:00,600
Make your toast.

178
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:01,559
Right, right, right.

179
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:03,879
Just two more words and I'm done.

180
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,240
What you eat doesn't matter.

181
00:09:05,759 --> 00:09:07,679
It's who you eat with that counts.

182
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:09,279
All my life,

183
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:10,759
I've lived by one principle:

184
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:12,440
It's good to make friends,

185
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:13,759
enjoy making friends,

186
00:09:14,039 --> 00:09:15,440
and make good friends.

187
00:09:16,639 --> 00:09:17,120
Come on, Dad.

188
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:17,759
Cheers.

189
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:20,320
That's so profound, Uncle.

190
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:21,000
Oh, not at all.

191
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,000
I'm rambling.

192
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:24,840
Say...

193
00:09:25,679 --> 00:09:26,960
The night of Cao Jun's accident,

194
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:27,639
what were you doing?

195
00:09:29,759 --> 00:09:31,320
Cao Jun?

196
00:09:33,759 --> 00:09:35,559
Didn't you know about that night?

197
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:36,879
I...

198
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:38,320
I was driving,

199
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:41,080
and that sculpture outside the factory gate...

200
00:09:41,399 --> 00:09:41,960
I crashed right into it.

201
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:42,960
Past two in the morning.

202
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:45,240
Points deducted,

203
00:09:45,679 --> 00:09:46,440
got fined,

204
00:09:47,159 --> 00:09:48,080
and they want compensation.

205
00:09:48,759 --> 00:09:49,639
I was really...

206
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:51,000
totally out of it.

207
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:51,840
My eyesight's bad.

208
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:54,080
What were you doing going back there so late?

209
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,000
No, no, no.

210
00:09:55,159 --> 00:09:55,679
I wasn't going to the factory.

211
00:09:55,679 --> 00:09:56,720
I... I...

212
00:09:57,519 --> 00:09:58,000
was going home.

213
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,159
Passed by there.

214
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:01,559
Once I got there, I got a bit dazed.

215
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:04,559
I completely lost my sense of direction.

216
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:05,960
Heading home from where?

217
00:10:08,639 --> 00:10:09,279
I... I...

218
00:10:09,279 --> 00:10:12,039
I had a few drinks at my son's place.

219
00:10:12,759 --> 00:10:13,600
Afterwards,

220
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,399
I took a nap.

221
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:16,799
Woke up around one o'clock.

222
00:10:17,879 --> 00:10:19,639
Thought I'd be fine.

223
00:10:20,039 --> 00:10:21,240
Thought I could drive.

224
00:10:21,799 --> 00:10:22,360
Besides,

225
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,720
hardly anyone's on the road that late.

226
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:27,240
So I drove home.

227
00:10:28,039 --> 00:10:29,480
But when I got near that spot,

228
00:10:30,159 --> 00:10:32,399
I started feeling dizzy and confused again.

229
00:10:33,279 --> 00:10:33,919
Anyway,

230
00:10:34,559 --> 00:10:35,639
just like that... bam!

231
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:37,080
You can't drink and drive.

232
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,240
Right, right.

233
00:10:38,519 --> 00:10:39,639
The traffic police already handled it.

234
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:42,879
Uncle,

235
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:45,159
do you still remember

236
00:10:45,399 --> 00:10:46,759
back during the '99 restructuring,

237
00:10:46,759 --> 00:10:47,600
the factory auctions?

238
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,840
You were in charge of many such projects.

239
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:57,639
That was all

240
00:10:58,879 --> 00:11:00,120
years ago.

241
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:02,480
Why do you ask?

242
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:04,799
We're making a promo video.

243
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:06,559
Right, right, right.

244
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:09,720
The documentary on Lapi Brewery back then—

245
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:10,720
you shot that, right?

246
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:11,879
Yes.

247
00:11:12,159 --> 00:11:12,799
"Malt Kingdom."

248
00:11:13,639 --> 00:11:14,279
Right, right, right.

249
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:15,360
I remember now.

250
00:11:15,799 --> 00:11:16,879
Xiaoqin showed it to me.

251
00:11:17,159 --> 00:11:17,879
You did a great job.

252
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:19,240
Thank you, Uncle.

253
00:11:20,759 --> 00:11:21,600
Uncle,

254
00:11:22,279 --> 00:11:24,799
were you close with Director Ma?

255
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,759
Xiaoqin loves spinach.

256
00:11:31,279 --> 00:11:31,799
Dad.

257
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:34,039
Leshui's asking you.

258
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,639
Were you close with Director Ma?

259
00:11:38,519 --> 00:11:39,320
Back then,

260
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,559
we had some work dealings.

261
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:42,919
A lot of people dealt with me back then.

262
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:45,759
Eat up, help yourself.

263
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:55,919
Sir,

264
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:58,720
do you remember Liu Xuemei?

265
00:11:59,519 --> 00:12:01,279
She was a beer taster at Lapi Brewery.

266
00:12:01,759 --> 00:12:04,679
Died on the street in the winter of 2000.

267
00:12:09,799 --> 00:12:10,600
I remember now.

268
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:11,639
Back then,

269
00:12:11,639 --> 00:12:12,519
it was in the news.

270
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:15,320
Heard she'd had too much to drink.

271
00:12:16,039 --> 00:12:16,720
Around here,

272
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:18,000
every winter, people getting drunk

273
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,360
and freezing to death by the road is common.

274
00:12:21,399 --> 00:12:21,960
So you see,

275
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:23,960
you should never overdrink.

276
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,960
Did you see Cao Jun before he died?

277
00:12:31,559 --> 00:12:32,279
Cao Jun?

278
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:34,840
Never mind before he died,

279
00:12:36,039 --> 00:12:36,759
well,

280
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,320
I hadn't seen him in years.

281
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,559
He was just a forklift driver,

282
00:12:40,679 --> 00:12:42,120
and he left the plant later on.

283
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:45,159
I was the brewery's chief engineer.

284
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,639
We never really had occasion to talk.

285
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:50,960
Where did chief engineer rank at the brewery?

286
00:12:53,159 --> 00:12:54,480
Can't really put a rank on it,

287
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:55,799
but, you know,

288
00:12:55,799 --> 00:12:56,919
when it came to the technical side,

289
00:12:59,000 --> 00:12:59,799
I was still the one...

290
00:12:59,799 --> 00:13:00,720
I called the shots.

291
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,480
As far as you recall,

292
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:09,480
did anyone have trouble with Qian Yichuan,

293
00:13:09,759 --> 00:13:10,519
Cao Jun,

294
00:13:10,519 --> 00:13:11,080
or Ma Guowen?

295
00:13:11,159 --> 00:13:11,879
Any clashes with them?

296
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,279
Qian Yichuan?

297
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:18,799
He was a gatekeeper at the old plant.

298
00:13:19,399 --> 00:13:20,919
Between him and me,

299
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,679
there was quite a distance.

300
00:13:23,519 --> 00:13:24,240
And I...

301
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,799
I didn't really know him well.

302
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,399
So I shouldn't speak out of turn.

303
00:13:28,039 --> 00:13:30,240
Now, Ma Guowen,

304
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:32,080
he had a bad temper.

305
00:13:32,679 --> 00:13:34,399
I actually butted heads with him a few times.

306
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:37,720
But that was all a long time ago.

307
00:13:38,799 --> 00:13:39,519
Anyway,

308
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:41,240
a man like me,

309
00:13:41,919 --> 00:13:43,039
I've always believed in

310
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,039
staying humble,

311
00:13:45,799 --> 00:13:46,679
respecting superiors,

312
00:13:46,919 --> 00:13:47,799
and caring for subordinates.

313
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:50,240
Back at the brewery,

314
00:13:50,799 --> 00:13:52,360
I was quite well-liked.

315
00:13:53,279 --> 00:13:55,240
You can ask around and check for yourselves.

316
00:13:57,639 --> 00:13:58,799
And another thing,

317
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:01,080
if you don't know

318
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:03,440
someone well enough,

319
00:14:04,159 --> 00:14:05,240
you shouldn't go talking reckless.

320
00:14:05,879 --> 00:14:06,360
Right?

321
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:16,120
Uncle,

322
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:18,159
have you seen the news lately?

323
00:14:19,519 --> 00:14:21,879
There's been a serial murder case at Lapi Brewery.

324
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:30,000
Catching criminals is the police's job.

325
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:33,600
Just because someone died at the brewery,

326
00:14:33,679 --> 00:14:34,559
doesn't mean we should connect it

327
00:14:34,559 --> 00:14:36,360
to the factory's sale back then.

328
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:40,840
Liu Xuemei?

329
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:41,799
I don't really remember her.

330
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:43,720
Back then,

331
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:44,600
factories like that,

332
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:45,480
there were plenty of them.

333
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:46,799
As for the factory,

334
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:47,360
selling it off,

335
00:14:47,759 --> 00:14:49,360
that wasn't the only one sold.

336
00:14:50,279 --> 00:14:50,840
Besides,

337
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:52,120
selling the brewery

338
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:54,120
was following national policy,

339
00:14:54,559 --> 00:14:56,159
pushing society forward, you know?

340
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:57,440
Uncle...

341
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:58,080
Leshui.

342
00:14:58,799 --> 00:14:59,960
I have some advice,

343
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:01,399
though I'm not sure if I should say it.

344
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,279
Go ahead, Uncle.

345
00:15:03,919 --> 00:15:05,240
I must remind you.

346
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,559
You're a journalist.

347
00:15:08,159 --> 00:15:09,440
Watch how you talk.

348
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:11,000
Know what to say

349
00:15:11,639 --> 00:15:13,200
and what not to say.

350
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:15,799
Don't go making mistakes.

351
00:15:21,159 --> 00:15:22,039
A glass of plain water.

352
00:15:22,919 --> 00:15:23,840
First, a bit of coloring.

353
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:29,960
Then add some alcohol.

354
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:31,360
Just a drop.

355
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,080
Too much of this knocks people out.

356
00:15:33,559 --> 00:15:35,440
Now, it's got no flavor, right?

357
00:15:38,519 --> 00:15:39,600
Beer flavoring.

358
00:15:42,519 --> 00:15:43,240
Just a splash.

359
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:45,320
Good.

360
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,480
Give it a stir first.

361
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,879
The color is even,

362
00:15:51,919 --> 00:15:53,000
but there's no foam.

363
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:55,480
Here's the crucial part.

364
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:57,240
A pinch of baking soda.

365
00:15:58,159 --> 00:15:59,000
Go easy on this stuff.

366
00:15:59,000 --> 00:15:59,960
Too much makes it too fizzy.

367
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:03,919
The most crucial step.

368
00:16:08,679 --> 00:16:09,159
Watch this.

369
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:16,679
Take a whiff.

370
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:19,799
Smells right, doesn't it?

371
00:16:21,919 --> 00:16:22,639
A pitcher of this

372
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:24,480
normally sells for 9.90.

373
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:25,600
How much do you make?

374
00:16:26,159 --> 00:16:26,840
A few cents, maybe.

375
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:28,480
Sell mine,

376
00:16:28,679 --> 00:16:29,399
and per glass,

377
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:31,080
you net eight bucks.

378
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:32,879
Eight bucks.

379
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,000
In this day and age,

380
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:36,600
you can't be too honest in business.

381
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,799
Be honest, and you won't make a dime.

382
00:16:38,159 --> 00:16:38,919
Look at mine—

383
00:16:42,159 --> 00:16:42,919
What "day and age"?

384
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,000
No matter the era, you don't rip people off!

385
00:16:47,559 --> 00:16:48,600
Don't rip people off?

386
00:16:48,679 --> 00:16:49,240
What's that supposed to mean?

387
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:50,799
Get out.

388
00:16:52,879 --> 00:16:53,240
What?

389
00:16:53,919 --> 00:16:54,279
Get lost.

390
00:16:55,039 --> 00:16:55,759
Piss off!

391
00:16:58,559 --> 00:16:59,799
You'll never amount to shit in this life!

392
00:17:03,759 --> 00:17:04,799
Move your car on your way out.

393
00:17:04,799 --> 00:17:05,440
It's in the way.

394
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:09,720
Tieping.

395
00:17:10,359 --> 00:17:10,839
Ignore him.

396
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,240
Get something to eat first.

397
00:17:14,039 --> 00:17:14,920
I already ate, Master.

398
00:17:15,799 --> 00:17:16,359
Don't worry about it.

399
00:17:16,359 --> 00:17:16,839
Go get some rest.

400
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,039
Master.

401
00:17:23,359 --> 00:17:24,039
I got paid today.

402
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:27,440
Go inside.

403
00:17:36,319 --> 00:17:36,759
Master.

404
00:17:37,319 --> 00:17:38,079
It's payday.

405
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:40,680
Look...

406
00:17:41,759 --> 00:17:42,680
Every time,

407
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,160
I've deposited it for you.

408
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:46,960
This time,

409
00:17:48,039 --> 00:17:48,839
go deposit it yourself.

410
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:51,319
After all, the money in the passbook

411
00:17:52,119 --> 00:17:52,920
is all yours.

412
00:17:53,839 --> 00:17:54,480
Wait, Master,

413
00:17:54,559 --> 00:17:56,000
I've never even been to a bank.

414
00:17:56,279 --> 00:17:57,319
You should still go.

415
00:17:57,559 --> 00:17:58,920
You can't rely on me forever.

416
00:18:00,319 --> 00:18:02,680
You have to learn to do things yourself.

417
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:04,039
Look,

418
00:18:05,599 --> 00:18:06,559
you have a long life ahead of you.

419
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,240
Go on. Do it yourself.

420
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:12,039
You should really go, Master.

421
00:18:13,119 --> 00:18:14,000
Hurry up.

422
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:14,920
Go.

423
00:18:31,759 --> 00:18:33,359
Layoffs are nothing to fear,

424
00:18:33,839 --> 00:18:36,200
the plant is always our home.

425
00:18:36,839 --> 00:18:38,880
Rejoin society with your own hands,

426
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:41,839
learn a skill to feed the family.

427
00:18:41,839 --> 00:18:43,400
The plant is always our home.

428
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:45,920
Rejoin society with your own hands,

429
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,960
learn a skill to feed the family.

430
00:18:48,799 --> 00:18:51,839
Vocational Training for Laid-Off Workers

431
00:18:52,519 --> 00:18:53,359
Did you sign up?

432
00:18:53,599 --> 00:18:54,440
Why would I sign up?

433
00:18:54,759 --> 00:18:55,680
If I sign up,

434
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:56,799
doesn't that mean I'm laid off?

435
00:18:56,799 --> 00:18:57,720
We don't even know the results yet.

436
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:58,359
I'm not going.

437
00:18:58,440 --> 00:18:59,119
How about we...

438
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:00,440
ask the director?

439
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:01,119
Right.

440
00:19:01,279 --> 00:19:01,839
Good idea.

441
00:19:01,839 --> 00:19:02,759
Let's go ask the director,

442
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:03,880
j-just to make sure.

443
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:04,559
Tieping,

444
00:19:04,559 --> 00:19:05,839
whatever you do, don't sign up.

445
00:19:05,839 --> 00:19:06,680
Don't fall for it.

446
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:07,559
Don't go.

447
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:13,920
Director! Director! Director!

448
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:15,839
What does this mean?

449
00:19:16,279 --> 00:19:16,680
Director,

450
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:17,799
got any insider info for us?

451
00:19:18,079 --> 00:19:18,480
Director,

452
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:20,839
is the layoff list out yet?

453
00:19:20,839 --> 00:19:21,960
Give us a hint, will you?

454
00:19:22,079 --> 00:19:22,400
Director,

455
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,759
we'll be fine, right?

456
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:25,720
Have you eaten?

457
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:26,839
Not yet.

458
00:19:27,359 --> 00:19:28,359
Go grab some food, then.

459
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,079
Can't work on an empty stomach.

460
00:19:31,559 --> 00:19:31,880
Go on.

461
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:33,920
Go, go, go.

462
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:36,119
Stop worrying over nothing.

463
00:19:40,519 --> 00:19:41,000
Master...

464
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:43,079
Why so glum?

465
00:19:46,799 --> 00:19:47,279
Come on.

466
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:49,519
I'll take you somewhere.

467
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:03,519
Shut the door.

468
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:05,519
It's freezing in here.

469
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:08,000
Nobody's been here in ages.

470
00:20:12,519 --> 00:20:13,799
When I was your age,

471
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:16,400
after clocking out every day,

472
00:20:16,559 --> 00:20:17,359
my master and the boys

473
00:20:17,359 --> 00:20:18,359
would bring me here to drink.

474
00:20:20,839 --> 00:20:21,400
I got drunk

475
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:22,240
and told my master,

476
00:20:23,079 --> 00:20:23,559
"Someday,

477
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:24,799
when I take an apprentice,

478
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:25,960
I'll bring him here to drink too."

479
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:28,880
This was our workshop's secret hideout.

480
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:31,400
Light the stove.

481
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:32,720
There's coal over there.

482
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:33,720
Hurry.

483
00:20:42,599 --> 00:20:43,799
I remember you came here before.

484
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:45,839
I did.

485
00:20:46,359 --> 00:20:47,480
My second year at the plant,

486
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:48,279
they locked this place up.

487
00:20:50,119 --> 00:20:50,839
I remember.

488
00:20:52,119 --> 00:20:52,880
Back then,

489
00:20:53,359 --> 00:20:54,119
you were just a kid.

490
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:04,599
You were tiny back then,

491
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:05,039
weren't you?

492
00:21:05,799 --> 00:21:06,880
Sitting tucked away in the corner.

493
00:21:08,519 --> 00:21:09,319
Old Xu was over there,

494
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:11,119
and Er Chengzi was over there.

495
00:21:11,119 --> 00:21:12,720
Er Chengzi pulled out that lighter,

496
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:13,720
messing with you.

497
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:14,960
He said

498
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:15,759
it wouldn't strike,

499
00:21:15,759 --> 00:21:16,720
and told you to take a look.

500
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:18,440
You leaned in,

501
00:21:18,559 --> 00:21:19,079
and snap!

502
00:21:20,519 --> 00:21:21,759
Nearly singed your eyebrows right off.

503
00:21:21,799 --> 00:21:22,240
Remember?

504
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:22,680
Yeah.

505
00:21:23,119 --> 00:21:24,119
You've got a great memory, Master.

506
00:21:29,759 --> 00:21:30,559
Think this is enough?

507
00:21:31,119 --> 00:21:31,480
Yeah.

508
00:21:31,519 --> 00:21:32,400
This'll do for now.

509
00:21:32,519 --> 00:21:34,480
Let's get the fire going first.

510
00:21:53,079 --> 00:21:53,400
Here.

511
00:21:56,599 --> 00:21:57,359
Have a drink,

512
00:21:57,359 --> 00:21:58,160
it'll warm you up.

513
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,200
Everyone says having a daughter is great,

514
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:12,240
that she's Daddy's little girl.

515
00:22:13,039 --> 00:22:14,000
Still...

516
00:22:14,319 --> 00:22:15,359
when it comes to having a drink,

517
00:22:15,799 --> 00:22:16,880
nothing beats having a son.

518
00:22:21,839 --> 00:22:22,519
Flip that over.

519
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:28,160
Tieping...

520
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:30,680
A couple days ago,

521
00:22:31,279 --> 00:22:32,640
Xiao Liang from the workshop said

522
00:22:33,079 --> 00:22:34,039
he wants to strike out on his own.

523
00:22:34,839 --> 00:22:35,720
Said his second uncle

524
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:37,240
chartered a big truck

525
00:22:37,279 --> 00:22:38,079
to help people move,

526
00:22:39,960 --> 00:22:41,119
make some money doing hard labor.

527
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:42,759
Once that gets going,

528
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:44,359
they'll be the founding crew.

529
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:47,599
He told me the other day,

530
00:22:49,319 --> 00:22:50,279
they need someone

531
00:22:51,519 --> 00:22:52,400
strong,

532
00:22:52,920 --> 00:22:53,720
honest and dependable,

533
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:57,880
someone who won't stir up any trouble.

534
00:22:58,759 --> 00:22:59,680
And looking at you,

535
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:01,119
you fit the bill completely.

536
00:23:03,319 --> 00:23:04,599
At my age,

537
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,960
they probably wouldn't want me anyway.

538
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:21,960
Look.

539
00:23:25,839 --> 00:23:26,559
I'm just

540
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:29,440
throwing out a hypothetical.

541
00:23:31,039 --> 00:23:31,559
Say,

542
00:23:33,039 --> 00:23:34,559
if the two of us got laid off,

543
00:23:35,319 --> 00:23:36,039
tell me,

544
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:38,279
what could we even do?

545
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:42,279
Master,

546
00:23:44,319 --> 00:23:45,079
what do you mean?

547
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:48,359
Just keeping a backup plan, that's all.

548
00:23:51,759 --> 00:23:52,480
Master,

549
00:23:54,880 --> 00:23:56,079
you want to turn in the list and take the money?

550
00:24:00,519 --> 00:24:01,599
It's not just me.

551
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:17,720
Master,

552
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:19,119
I'm definitely not taking this money.

553
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:21,119
Whoever wants this money

554
00:24:21,599 --> 00:24:22,160
can come get it from me.

555
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:34,240
What are you doing?

556
00:24:35,079 --> 00:24:35,960
I can scrape up more later.

557
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:37,799
Every month's pay,

558
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:39,119
I'll give it all to you.

559
00:24:39,960 --> 00:24:40,759
It'll be enough sooner or later.

560
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:44,039
Where did you get this money?

561
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:47,599
All your monthly wages are with me.

562
00:24:48,400 --> 00:24:49,680
Where did you get this kind of cash?

563
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:56,240
Tieping.

564
00:24:57,759 --> 00:25:00,319
Have you gotten mixed up with shady people?

565
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:08,680
Those hoodlums...

566
00:25:09,359 --> 00:25:10,240
what did they get you into?

567
00:25:12,559 --> 00:25:13,440
I'm asking you!

568
00:25:14,039 --> 00:25:14,599
Answer me!

569
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:16,240
No, Master.

570
00:25:39,599 --> 00:25:40,240
It's delicious.

571
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:56,960
How long has it been since you had a proper meal?

572
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:07,640
Are you stupid?

573
00:26:09,160 --> 00:26:10,359
You're still growing.

574
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:12,079
How much can you really

575
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:13,240
save by skimping on food?

576
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:29,880
Tieping,

577
00:26:32,559 --> 00:26:33,559
about getting laid off,

578
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:35,880
we've got to be prepared.

579
00:26:39,799 --> 00:26:40,759
But whatever we do,

580
00:26:42,480 --> 00:26:43,559
we can't let ourselves starve.

581
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:05,319
Master,

582
00:27:06,759 --> 00:27:07,519
I don't want to leave.

583
00:27:09,640 --> 00:27:10,799
I just want to work at the factory.

584
00:27:12,240 --> 00:27:13,160
I just want to be a worker.

585
00:27:23,640 --> 00:27:24,519
I'm not leaving anyway.

586
00:27:25,519 --> 00:27:26,559
What are they gonna do?

587
00:27:30,839 --> 00:27:31,599
We're just not leaving.

588
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:54,400
Right.

589
00:27:54,920 --> 00:27:55,680
We're not leaving.

590
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:57,559
Let's see what he can do. Appliance Repair,

591
00:27:57,839 --> 00:27:58,680
and Auto Repair

592
00:27:58,799 --> 00:27:59,599
are already full.

593
00:28:00,279 --> 00:28:01,759
Pedicure and Reflexology Class

594
00:28:01,880 --> 00:28:03,440
has only three spots left.

595
00:28:03,519 --> 00:28:04,640
Register now.

596
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:06,039
Attention, fellow workers.

597
00:28:08,519 --> 00:28:09,279
Look,

598
00:28:09,480 --> 00:28:11,079
I know you all have

599
00:28:11,519 --> 00:28:12,640
deep feelings for our factory.

600
00:28:13,920 --> 00:28:15,319
But Lapi Brewery right now...

601
00:28:15,839 --> 00:28:16,960
You all know our situation.

602
00:28:17,799 --> 00:28:19,680
Restructuring has truly become inevitable.

603
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:20,720
We're overstaffed,

604
00:28:20,759 --> 00:28:21,440
heavily burdened,

605
00:28:21,440 --> 00:28:22,759
and productivity just won't rise.

606
00:28:22,960 --> 00:28:23,400
Therefore,

607
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:25,640
some people must make sacrifices.

608
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:26,319
Enough!

609
00:28:26,319 --> 00:28:27,519
Just read the list already.

610
00:28:27,519 --> 00:28:28,640
Stop stalling.

611
00:28:28,759 --> 00:28:29,279
Honestly.

612
00:28:29,359 --> 00:28:29,920
Fine, then.

613
00:28:30,079 --> 00:28:31,200
Since you're in a hurry, I'll read it.

614
00:28:32,039 --> 00:28:32,680
Publicity Department:

615
00:28:32,839 --> 00:28:33,640
Zhao Haipeng.

616
00:28:35,240 --> 00:28:35,759
Women's Federation:

617
00:28:35,960 --> 00:28:36,799
Tian Meihua.

618
00:28:38,319 --> 00:28:39,240
Finance Department:

619
00:28:39,319 --> 00:28:40,000
Qian Yichuan,

620
00:28:40,119 --> 00:28:40,640
Tu Chunyan.

621
00:28:41,039 --> 00:28:41,559
Logistics:

622
00:28:41,839 --> 00:28:42,519
Zhang Yuming.

623
00:28:42,720 --> 00:28:43,519
Forklift Team:

624
00:28:43,799 --> 00:28:44,480
Cao Jun,

625
00:28:44,880 --> 00:28:45,599
Wu Aigong.

626
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:46,680
Inspection Department...

627
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:47,519
I'm not leaving!

628
00:28:48,039 --> 00:28:48,960
None of us is leaving!

629
00:28:50,119 --> 00:28:51,400
This factory doesn't belong to you alone!

630
00:28:51,839 --> 00:28:52,680
Why should we leave?

631
00:28:52,839 --> 00:28:53,599
What are you doing?

632
00:28:55,759 --> 00:28:56,480
Security!

633
00:28:56,599 --> 00:28:56,920
Here!

634
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:57,240
Tieping!

635
00:28:57,440 --> 00:28:58,240
What are you doing?

636
00:28:59,319 --> 00:28:59,880
What do you think you're doing?

637
00:29:00,359 --> 00:29:00,720
Tieping!

638
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:02,359
The factory belongs to all of us!

639
00:29:02,480 --> 00:29:03,519
We won't leave! What can you do?

640
00:29:03,519 --> 00:29:04,000
Who let you in?

641
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:04,880
Take him to the police station!

642
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:05,839
Hurry up!

643
00:29:05,920 --> 00:29:06,920
Let go of me!

644
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:08,759
Tieping, what are you doing?

645
00:29:09,119 --> 00:29:10,079
What do you want? I'm not leaving!

646
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:12,440
Director!

647
00:29:12,559 --> 00:29:13,480
I don't know what's gotten into this kid.

648
00:29:14,039 --> 00:29:14,559
I'll handle him.

649
00:29:14,839 --> 00:29:15,759
I'll take him back and discipline him.

650
00:29:16,119 --> 00:29:16,799
Come on, let go.

651
00:29:17,240 --> 00:29:17,799
Cheng Youtian,

652
00:29:17,799 --> 00:29:18,160
Let go!

653
00:29:18,759 --> 00:29:20,599
with an apprentice like this,

654
00:29:20,839 --> 00:29:22,440
the factory definitely can't keep him!

655
00:29:23,039 --> 00:29:23,440
Director!

656
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:24,759
Let go!

657
00:29:24,759 --> 00:29:26,680
Let go! Let go!

658
00:29:27,440 --> 00:29:27,839
Let go!

659
00:29:27,839 --> 00:29:28,559
Let go!

660
00:29:29,039 --> 00:29:29,839
Let go!

661
00:29:30,039 --> 00:29:31,119
Let go!

662
00:29:31,799 --> 00:29:32,599
Let go!

663
00:29:45,960 --> 00:29:46,920
The kid doesn't know any better.

664
00:29:47,559 --> 00:29:48,519
I apologize on his behalf.

665
00:29:49,119 --> 00:29:50,039
The country has laws,

666
00:29:50,039 --> 00:29:51,039
and the factory has rules.

667
00:29:51,440 --> 00:29:53,039
A bad master breeds a bad apprentice.

668
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:54,519
You raised an apprentice like this,

669
00:29:54,559 --> 00:29:55,640
so what's the point of kneeling?

670
00:29:57,079 --> 00:29:57,400
Right.

671
00:29:58,839 --> 00:29:59,519
It's all my fault.

672
00:30:00,599 --> 00:30:01,240
It's on me.

673
00:30:02,680 --> 00:30:03,319
This kid...

674
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:05,240
He grew up in an orphanage.

675
00:30:06,559 --> 00:30:07,400
He treats the factory as his home,

676
00:30:07,599 --> 00:30:08,599
and sees us as his parents.

677
00:30:09,759 --> 00:30:10,839
He has no other skills.

678
00:30:12,079 --> 00:30:14,880
He just wants to be an honest worker.

679
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:17,160
Please keep him at the factory.

680
00:30:17,680 --> 00:30:18,519
Let him stay.

681
00:30:20,519 --> 00:30:21,440
Punish him however you want,

682
00:30:21,440 --> 00:30:22,400
just let him stay.

683
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:24,079
Don't send him to the police.

684
00:30:24,599 --> 00:30:25,680
If he gets a criminal record,

685
00:30:26,519 --> 00:30:28,079
his whole life is ruined.

686
00:30:30,680 --> 00:30:31,799
I'm begging you.

687
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:32,400
Master.

688
00:30:32,559 --> 00:30:33,200
Get up.

689
00:30:33,359 --> 00:30:34,440
Don't beg him.

690
00:30:34,640 --> 00:30:35,880
Don't beg him!

691
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:37,640
Don't move!

692
00:30:38,279 --> 00:30:38,839
Tieping,

693
00:30:41,400 --> 00:30:42,119
apologize right now!

694
00:30:47,079 --> 00:30:48,079
Your parents died young,

695
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:50,640
and I failed to raise you right.

696
00:30:52,680 --> 00:30:53,680
Disrespecting the leadership...

697
00:30:54,319 --> 00:30:55,279
You have no manners!

698
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:58,240
Apologize to him right now!

699
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:04,799
Apologize!

700
00:31:07,119 --> 00:31:07,799
Fine.

701
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:09,880
If you won't apologize,

702
00:31:15,519 --> 00:31:16,200
I'll leave.

703
00:31:19,079 --> 00:31:20,640
I won't stay at this factory either!

704
00:31:24,640 --> 00:31:25,359
Master!

705
00:31:27,640 --> 00:31:28,440
I'm sorry.

706
00:31:28,960 --> 00:31:29,759
I'm sorry, Director.

707
00:31:30,319 --> 00:31:31,039
I was wrong.

708
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:33,519
Louder!

709
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:34,680
Let everyone hear you!

710
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:38,680
I'm sorry, Director!

711
00:31:39,119 --> 00:31:40,319
I was wrong!

712
00:31:40,519 --> 00:31:42,400
This has nothing to do with my master!

713
00:31:42,640 --> 00:31:43,960
I apologize to you!

714
00:31:44,160 --> 00:31:45,559
I shouldn't have run my mouth!

715
00:31:56,799 --> 00:31:57,519
All right, that's enough.

716
00:31:57,759 --> 00:31:58,559
Let him go back to the factory.

717
00:31:58,720 --> 00:31:59,200
Back to the workshop.

718
00:31:59,200 --> 00:31:59,839
Get him back inside.

719
00:32:00,039 --> 00:32:00,640
Piss off!

720
00:32:07,559 --> 00:32:07,839
Let's go.

721
00:32:16,440 --> 00:32:17,200
Cheng Youtian.

722
00:32:18,720 --> 00:32:19,519
Hold on a second.

723
00:32:20,119 --> 00:32:21,279
I want to have a word with you.

724
00:32:23,039 --> 00:32:23,720
Jianguo.

725
00:32:24,440 --> 00:32:24,880
Old Ge.

726
00:32:25,799 --> 00:32:26,519
Take Tieping back.

727
00:32:27,359 --> 00:32:27,920
Back to the workshop.

728
00:32:28,279 --> 00:32:28,960
Take him back.

729
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:29,920
Move.

730
00:32:32,720 --> 00:32:33,720
Cheng Youtian...

731
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:37,440
You're truly Lapi Brewery's model worker.

732
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:41,519
Quite impressive, aren't you?

733
00:32:44,799 --> 00:32:45,599
Thank you, Director.

734
00:32:47,759 --> 00:32:48,480
What're you doing?

735
00:32:49,880 --> 00:32:52,000
I think I heard you say just now

736
00:32:52,160 --> 00:32:53,799
that you won't work in this factory anymore.

737
00:32:53,799 --> 00:32:54,599
Right?

738
00:32:56,759 --> 00:32:57,839
Everyone here heard it, too.

739
00:32:57,839 --> 00:32:58,480
Didn't you?

740
00:32:58,759 --> 00:32:59,160
Right.

741
00:33:05,640 --> 00:33:06,599
I will now announce

742
00:33:07,160 --> 00:33:09,480
the bottling workshop layoff list.

743
00:33:09,880 --> 00:33:11,359
Cheng Youtian.

744
00:33:56,079 --> 00:33:57,000
Old classmate,

745
00:33:57,240 --> 00:33:59,119
there's nothing left for you in this case.

746
00:33:59,599 --> 00:34:00,599
Why haven't you gone back to Beijing yet?

747
00:34:02,359 --> 00:34:04,119
How come you had time to ask me out today?

748
00:34:05,680 --> 00:34:07,279
How do you guys usually solve cases?

749
00:34:09,239 --> 00:34:09,960
Interviewing me?

750
00:34:11,239 --> 00:34:12,119
Well, asking me about this,

751
00:34:12,559 --> 00:34:13,360
you've come to the right guy.

752
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:14,920
When it comes to solving cases,

753
00:34:15,960 --> 00:34:16,559
there are no shortcuts.

754
00:34:17,880 --> 00:34:19,480
It's a real grind.

755
00:34:19,880 --> 00:34:21,079
Evidence,

756
00:34:21,079 --> 00:34:22,199
testimonies,

757
00:34:22,199 --> 00:34:23,280
clues,

758
00:34:23,280 --> 00:34:24,360
interview transcripts...

759
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:25,559
You have to comb through them over and over.

760
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:26,880
It gets on my nerves.

761
00:34:27,320 --> 00:34:28,119
And sometimes,

762
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:30,199
you just have to bite the bullet and ask.

763
00:34:30,480 --> 00:34:32,119
You question the same person repeatedly,

764
00:34:32,119 --> 00:34:33,440
"Why did you do that?"

765
00:34:33,880 --> 00:34:35,840
Then from what they say,

766
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:37,119
you catch their contradictions.

767
00:34:37,760 --> 00:34:38,880
Anyway, as long as you put in the effort

768
00:34:39,239 --> 00:34:40,320
and investigate thoroughly,

769
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:42,599
you'll definitely figure it out.

770
00:34:43,159 --> 00:34:44,320
So what is our line of work about?

771
00:34:44,559 --> 00:34:45,599
Hunting for tiny clues,

772
00:34:46,039 --> 00:34:46,719
panning for gold in the sand.

773
00:34:48,360 --> 00:34:49,760
Good, then I did the right thing.

774
00:34:50,719 --> 00:34:51,320
What did you do?

775
00:34:55,320 --> 00:34:56,599
Do you know when Gao Xuelin

776
00:34:56,679 --> 00:34:58,280
joined your police force?

777
00:35:00,719 --> 00:35:01,480
Why are you asking about that?

778
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:04,360
I've been to his hometown.

779
00:35:05,239 --> 00:35:05,960
Over the past few years,

780
00:35:06,119 --> 00:35:07,000
he kept coming to Lacheng.

781
00:35:07,719 --> 00:35:08,719
His transfer to Lacheng

782
00:35:09,039 --> 00:35:10,000
was definitely premeditated.

783
00:35:21,159 --> 00:35:22,440
Look at how busy you are,

784
00:35:23,320 --> 00:35:24,559
even investigating us cops.

785
00:35:26,719 --> 00:35:27,679
Look at him.

786
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:28,920
Whenever he investigates,

787
00:35:28,920 --> 00:35:31,079
he's fixated on things from ten years ago.

788
00:35:32,840 --> 00:35:35,119
He asks everyone about Liu Xuemei's death.

789
00:35:37,159 --> 00:35:37,840
The way he questions people,

790
00:35:38,159 --> 00:35:38,760
the way he acts,

791
00:35:39,639 --> 00:35:40,679
it's all very strange.

792
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:43,199
Don't you think something's off?

793
00:35:55,960 --> 00:35:57,559
Gao Xuelin's father was Gao Wusong,

794
00:35:58,199 --> 00:35:58,880
from Qingzhou.

795
00:35:59,239 --> 00:36:00,239
A cab driver.

796
00:36:01,239 --> 00:36:03,039
On December 31, 1999,

797
00:36:03,920 --> 00:36:04,960
he drove a passenger

798
00:36:05,199 --> 00:36:06,440
from Qingzhou to Lacheng.

799
00:36:06,599 --> 00:36:07,599
On the way back,

800
00:36:08,639 --> 00:36:09,559
due to drunk driving,

801
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:11,920
he died in a crash.

802
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:18,679
Do you know who his passenger was?

803
00:36:19,679 --> 00:36:20,599
Most likely,

804
00:36:20,960 --> 00:36:21,960
it was Liu Xuemei.

805
00:36:24,079 --> 00:36:25,119
On that exact same day,

806
00:36:25,920 --> 00:36:29,599
both died because of alcohol.

807
00:36:29,920 --> 00:36:30,960
Don't you find that strange?

808
00:36:34,880 --> 00:36:36,360
Gao Xuelin knows all about this.

809
00:36:37,599 --> 00:36:38,719
Did he ever report it to you?

810
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:48,639
You're pretty professional.

811
00:36:48,639 --> 00:36:49,039
Seriously.

812
00:36:49,480 --> 00:36:50,320
I took it all in.

813
00:36:50,800 --> 00:36:51,639
You're really something.

814
00:36:51,880 --> 00:36:52,559
Well,

815
00:36:53,159 --> 00:36:54,039
thanks, old classmate.

816
00:36:54,320 --> 00:36:55,440
These clues you provided,

817
00:36:55,960 --> 00:36:56,840
I'll write them down in a bit.

818
00:37:01,440 --> 00:37:02,079
Say,

819
00:37:02,679 --> 00:37:04,119
maybe install a camera at home?

820
00:37:05,119 --> 00:37:06,800
I think that'd be a great idea.

821
00:37:07,039 --> 00:37:07,840
Good to be security-conscious.

822
00:37:08,639 --> 00:37:09,679
Living on your own out here,

823
00:37:09,880 --> 00:37:10,679
it's best to be careful.

824
00:37:28,280 --> 00:37:28,880
Let me

825
00:37:28,880 --> 00:37:29,639
propose a toast.

826
00:37:30,800 --> 00:37:33,800
Chen Yuan will make grade dean this year?

827
00:37:34,199 --> 00:37:35,679
Dad, I'm working on it.

828
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:36,400
Good.

829
00:37:37,119 --> 00:37:39,000
Did Xiaohu get elected class monitor?

830
00:37:39,639 --> 00:37:41,079
Grandpa, I don't want to be class monitor.

831
00:37:42,159 --> 00:37:43,679
Then what do you want to be?

832
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:44,280
A boss.

833
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:46,840
When you grow up,

834
00:37:46,840 --> 00:37:47,880
you should be like your grandpa

835
00:37:48,559 --> 00:37:49,239
and become a director.

836
00:37:50,480 --> 00:37:51,119
Come on, come on.

837
00:37:51,119 --> 00:37:52,559
Cheers.

838
00:37:52,559 --> 00:37:53,079
Here, Xiaohu.

839
00:37:53,440 --> 00:37:53,880
Here.

840
00:38:00,480 --> 00:38:01,400
Eat up.

841
00:38:04,360 --> 00:38:05,199
Xiaohu.

842
00:38:06,159 --> 00:38:06,719
Dad.

843
00:38:07,400 --> 00:38:08,159
Lately,

844
00:38:08,280 --> 00:38:10,039
stay away from Lapi Brewery.

845
00:38:10,599 --> 00:38:11,599
Especially at night.

846
00:38:11,719 --> 00:38:12,360
It's not safe.

847
00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:14,960
Dad, you too.

848
00:38:15,199 --> 00:38:16,320
Don't wander around alone so much.

849
00:38:20,639 --> 00:38:21,159
By the way,

850
00:38:21,880 --> 00:38:22,400
Dad,

851
00:38:22,840 --> 00:38:24,039
do you remember Cao Jun?

852
00:38:25,360 --> 00:38:26,719
Cao Jun from Lapi Brewery.

853
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:28,239
Isn't he dead?

854
00:38:29,239 --> 00:38:29,800
Yeah.

855
00:38:30,760 --> 00:38:31,559
A while ago,

856
00:38:31,760 --> 00:38:32,840
he wandered into our school,

857
00:38:32,960 --> 00:38:34,079
and the security guards kicked him out.

858
00:38:35,920 --> 00:38:37,079
What was he doing at your school?

859
00:38:37,239 --> 00:38:38,159
Beats me.

860
00:38:39,360 --> 00:38:39,920
Chen Yuan,

861
00:38:40,559 --> 00:38:41,679
back then,

862
00:38:41,679 --> 00:38:43,159
a good position was saved for you,

863
00:38:43,440 --> 00:38:44,239
yet you insisted

864
00:38:44,599 --> 00:38:46,880
on roughing it as a teacher.

865
00:38:47,320 --> 00:38:47,880
Of course,

866
00:38:48,079 --> 00:38:49,880
being a teacher is pretty good nowadays too.

867
00:38:51,320 --> 00:38:51,920
Dad,

868
00:38:52,400 --> 00:38:53,719
I actually enjoy teaching.

869
00:38:55,239 --> 00:38:56,039
I'd say

870
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:59,599
you should've listened to Director Zheng back then.

871
00:39:01,159 --> 00:39:02,599
Here, let me toast to you.

872
00:39:04,119 --> 00:39:04,960
I'm retired now.

873
00:39:05,159 --> 00:39:06,719
Just an idle old man these days.

874
00:39:07,480 --> 00:39:08,559
Retired or not, you're still the Director.

875
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:20,400
Does it still itch here?

876
00:39:21,119 --> 00:39:21,920
To the left. To the left.

877
00:39:22,679 --> 00:39:24,840
I went home and cleaned out the back room today.

878
00:39:24,960 --> 00:39:25,760
It's super spacious now.

879
00:39:27,079 --> 00:39:28,599
You should've spent that time resting.

880
00:39:29,119 --> 00:39:30,599
I've rested for plenty of years.

881
00:39:30,920 --> 00:39:32,320
I actually want to keep busy.

882
00:39:33,480 --> 00:39:35,400
I'll check Chunli's hair salon tomorrow.

883
00:39:35,800 --> 00:39:37,280
She happens to need a shampooer.

884
00:39:37,320 --> 00:39:38,800
It pays 3,000 a month.

885
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:40,320
Shift work, too.

886
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:42,239
In my free time, I can find other work.

887
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:43,880
All right, all right.

888
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:44,400
Stop scratching.

889
00:39:44,559 --> 00:39:45,000
That's enough.

890
00:39:45,079 --> 00:39:46,400
Go find the nurse.

891
00:39:46,480 --> 00:39:47,079
Let's get discharged.

892
00:39:47,280 --> 00:39:48,119
You haven't fully recovered yet.

893
00:39:48,119 --> 00:39:49,079
Where would you go?

894
00:39:49,280 --> 00:39:49,840
Good grief.

895
00:39:49,880 --> 00:39:51,159
Every day here costs money!

896
00:39:53,039 --> 00:39:53,880
I've made up my mind.

897
00:39:55,639 --> 00:39:56,440
I'm not staying here anymore.

898
00:39:56,800 --> 00:39:57,679
Leave this place.

899
00:39:59,039 --> 00:40:00,000
Leave this place?

900
00:40:00,880 --> 00:40:01,679
Where to?

901
00:40:02,679 --> 00:40:03,480
Facing the sea,

902
00:40:03,559 --> 00:40:04,599
where spring flowers bloom.

903
00:40:06,039 --> 00:40:06,960
Hainan?

904
00:40:07,079 --> 00:40:08,199
Forget Hainan.

905
00:40:08,239 --> 00:40:08,800
Sanya.

906
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:09,960
Are you stupid?

907
00:40:09,960 --> 00:40:11,280
Isn't Sanya in Hainan?

908
00:40:11,639 --> 00:40:12,159
Is it?

909
00:40:13,440 --> 00:40:14,079
So what?

910
00:40:14,760 --> 00:40:15,800
It's so far away.

911
00:40:15,880 --> 00:40:16,880
You going alone?

912
00:40:17,480 --> 00:40:18,719
Why, you're not coming?

913
00:40:21,119 --> 00:40:22,639
You haven't officially invited me.

914
00:40:23,079 --> 00:40:24,800
Should I send you an invitation?

915
00:40:25,280 --> 00:40:26,440
Knowing your nature,

916
00:40:26,760 --> 00:40:27,239
all I have to do is whistle,

917
00:40:27,239 --> 00:40:28,559
and you'll come hopping right over.

918
00:40:30,119 --> 00:40:31,559
Wanna bet I'll douse you?

919
00:40:34,199 --> 00:40:35,000
Seriously, though,

920
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:36,360
once you're discharged,

921
00:40:36,760 --> 00:40:38,239
get a haircut

922
00:40:38,559 --> 00:40:39,639
and shave your beard.

923
00:40:40,039 --> 00:40:41,599
You don't look like a decent guy.

924
00:40:41,840 --> 00:40:43,719
Being clean-cut doesn't make you a good guy.

925
00:40:43,719 --> 00:40:44,800
Keep talking nonsense.

926
00:40:46,880 --> 00:40:47,400
What?

927
00:40:47,840 --> 00:40:49,320
Got standards for my looks again?

928
00:40:49,559 --> 00:40:50,559
You bet.

929
00:40:51,679 --> 00:40:53,719
You need to clean up nice and sharp,

930
00:40:54,639 --> 00:40:55,559
just like back then,

931
00:40:55,840 --> 00:40:57,119
when you worked in accounting.

932
00:40:57,559 --> 00:40:58,559
What was I like back then?

933
00:40:59,280 --> 00:41:00,000
Super handsome.

934
00:41:00,440 --> 00:41:01,800
The handsomest guy in the factory.

935
00:41:01,920 --> 00:41:04,119
So you were just after my good looks back then.

936
00:41:04,360 --> 00:41:05,280
You're pretty shallow.

937
00:41:05,559 --> 00:41:07,000
And you're not?

938
00:41:07,760 --> 00:41:09,159
Wasn't I the prettiest in the factory too?

939
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:10,559
Truth be told,

940
00:41:10,960 --> 00:41:12,920
you really were the hottest girl in our factory.

941
00:41:13,320 --> 00:41:14,480
Nonsense.

942
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:16,800
Back then, you all said Liu Xuemei

943
00:41:16,800 --> 00:41:18,079
was the factory belle.

944
00:41:18,079 --> 00:41:19,079
I never said that.

945
00:41:19,119 --> 00:41:20,360
Liu Xuemei acted all smug every day,

946
00:41:20,360 --> 00:41:21,360
flirting with everyone she met.

947
00:41:21,440 --> 00:41:22,639
She didn't even know how to smile.

948
00:41:22,679 --> 00:41:23,840
Her face looked like a sweet potato.

949
00:41:23,840 --> 00:41:24,559
You were the one...

950
00:41:24,559 --> 00:41:25,320
who called her the factory belle.

951
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:26,239
I called her the factory belle

952
00:41:26,239 --> 00:41:27,440
so everyone rushed after her,

953
00:41:27,559 --> 00:41:28,800
and left you for me.

954
00:41:29,719 --> 00:41:30,599
You idiot.

955
00:41:32,440 --> 00:41:32,960
Yan.

956
00:41:33,719 --> 00:41:34,559
Tieping is here.

957
00:41:35,039 --> 00:41:36,400
My... My master stewed an old hen.

958
00:41:36,559 --> 00:41:37,400
I brought it over on my way.

959
00:41:37,559 --> 00:41:38,320
Sneaking in so quietly.

960
00:41:38,400 --> 00:41:39,199
Thanks.

961
00:41:40,239 --> 00:41:41,360
It's not postpartum recovery,

962
00:41:41,719 --> 00:41:42,880
why chicken soup?

963
00:41:44,079 --> 00:41:45,239
Just thank him.

964
00:41:45,239 --> 00:41:46,800
He stewed chicken for you and you're complaining?

965
00:41:47,239 --> 00:41:47,760
This guy...

966
00:41:49,559 --> 00:41:50,199
Tieping,

967
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:52,599
tell your master when you get back

968
00:41:52,960 --> 00:41:54,119
that the two of us are going to Sanya.

969
00:41:54,559 --> 00:41:55,480
Ask him if he wants to come.

970
00:41:55,719 --> 00:41:56,800
If he does, we can go together.

971
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:58,480
It's super warm over there in winter.

972
00:41:58,679 --> 00:42:00,199
Everyone swims shirtless.

973
00:42:00,639 --> 00:42:01,480
When you're free,

974
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:03,400
when you go to the bathhouse,

975
00:42:03,400 --> 00:42:04,280
practice holding your breath.

976
00:42:04,840 --> 00:42:05,960
Why would I practice holding my breath?

977
00:42:06,360 --> 00:42:07,320
In case I fall into the sea,

978
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:08,239
so you can fish me out!

979
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:10,719
No way am I doing that.

980
00:42:10,920 --> 00:42:12,239
I just want to see how you swim.

981
00:42:12,559 --> 00:42:13,920
What swimming style can a lame guy have?

982
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:14,760
Just spinning around in circles,

983
00:42:14,760 --> 00:42:15,440
over and over.

984
00:42:15,440 --> 00:42:16,400
You silly fool.

985
00:42:16,440 --> 00:42:17,320
Your leg is all better?

986
00:42:17,320 --> 00:42:18,000
It's fine now.

987
00:42:18,639 --> 00:42:19,360
You silly idiot.

988
00:42:19,360 --> 00:42:20,440
Drink it while it's hot.

989
00:42:20,559 --> 00:42:21,719
Which ward is Qian Yichuan in?

990
00:42:21,920 --> 00:42:23,000
Room 208, Bed 16.

991
00:42:23,440 --> 00:42:23,880
Thanks.

992
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:26,559
Tieping.

993
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:47,039
Get off me.

994
00:42:48,639 --> 00:42:49,800
If he doesn't cherish you...

995
00:42:50,159 --> 00:42:51,280
I cherish you!

996
00:42:52,599 --> 00:42:53,280
I cherish you.
